585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 506 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Ruth Marcus, who established the Ben and Ruth Marcus Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Ruth Marcus was a champion of women here in Muskegon County for nearly half a century. Through her work as a board member at Muskegon Community College, Community Mental Health, Every Woman's Place, and Muskegon Area Planned Parenthood, she served as an advocate for women, inspiring them to pursue higher education, to take a greater role in the political arena, and to let their voice be heard in important causes. Her husband, Ben, was a leading worker's compensation attorney and a pioneer in this field. Ben Marcus came to Muskegon after World War II, a time when over 50 workers a year were dying in Muskegon Foundries due to lung disease. In 1995, he was inducted into the Michigan Worker's Hall of Fame and received the State Bar of Michigan's Champion of Justice Award. His work on behalf of Michigan's workers will remain a strong legacy in the field of labor law. The Marcus' Fund will provide financial assistance to area students who will attend Muskegon Community College.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
