/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 508 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Charles and Jessie Goodnow, who established the Charles and Jessie Goodnow Educational Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Sometimes, it is the very quiet people who ask for little but, through their generosity, truly make a difference in the world. Charles and Jessie Goodnow had vacationed in Muskegon for years and loved the area so much that they moved here in the 1930s and made Muskegon their home. Although neither of them attended college, both appreciated the value of education. The Goodnows lived an austere lifestyle that enabled them to build a sizable estate, and since they had no children of their own, they chose to use their estate to make a gift of education to Muskegon area students. The Goodnows produced this gift by creating the Community Foundation's first scholarship. The income from this fund has awarded over one and a half million dollars in scholarships to Muskegon youth, continuing to grant Charles and Jessie Goodnow's lasting gift of education to the current and future generations of Muskegon County youth.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
