/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of the Robert M. Cutler family, who established the Cutler Family Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Robert Cutler was a retired Howmet executive and a former County Commissioner. His wife, Betsy, taught and provided counseling for 19 years at Reeths-Puffer High School while also serving as President of the Michigan Pine and Dunes Girl Scout Council. The Cutlers both devoted themselves to community activism and highly valued education. Accordingly, they wanted to make a gift to help young people in the community pursue higher education. This inspiration became the Cutler Family Scholarship through a gift to the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. The award is for a Reeths-Puffer graduate who excels in math and/or science and plans to pursue a degree in either of these disciplines. By creating this scholarship, the Cutlers elevated their regard for education into a lasting reality, granting the youth of their community a permanent gift of education.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
