686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 511 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Richard C. Goodspeed, who established the Effah Elizabeth Ferris Scholarship in honor of Effah Elizabeth Ferris. Richard Goodspeed originally established the scholarship through the Muskegon Bank and Trust Company. Later, it was transferred to the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Effah Elizabeth Ferris graduated from Whitehall High School in 1901. Before this time, she had lost both of her parents. The people of Whitehall took her in when she had no money or place to go. Effah Elizabeth Ferris went on to graduate from college and become a teacher, a rare achievement in those days. Even with these admirable accomplishments, through the years, Effah Elizabeth Ferris would always remember the kindness displayed by the people of Whitehall. This scholarship honors that kindness and materializes Effah Elizabeth Ferris' thankfulness for the gift of compassion she received.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
