/P 512 0 R
/E (This scholarship was established by Irene Herremans in honor of Eleanor and Albert Herremans through the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Albert immigrated from Belgium at age 13 and settled in Ravenna, where he later returned after serving in WWII in the Philippines. He and Eleanor \(Link\) Herremans, a lifelong Ravenna resident, married and ran a dairy farm together, sharing the work and a deep respect for the land. They valued education and encouraged their children and grandchildren to pursue meaningful careers. To honor their legacy and love of the natural environment, this scholarship supports Ravenna High School seniors pursuing studies in agriculture, animal care, natural resources, environmental fields, or related areas.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
