/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 514 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Marjorie B. Dekker, who established the Herman C. & Marjorie B. Dekker Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Marjorie had been a teacher for Muskegon Public Schools for 22 years and had formerly served as Secretary of Cedar Creek Township. She was a member of Unity Reformed Church since 1940, the Winsome Class, RCWM \(President\), Muskegon Classis RCWM \(President\), M.E.A.- R, Greater Muskegon Woman's Club, Johnson Hall Seniors, and Muskegon County Republican Women. She served as a Hackley Hospital Volunteer, a Co-Coordinator for the MHS Class of 1935, and as a substitute teacher. Marjorie received Mother of the Year honors in 1986 and Michigan Mother of the Year honors in 1987. Marjorie enjoyed shopping and sewing, and she has many interests in arts and crafts in her spare time. She also enjoyed traveling and arranging trips for her school students. Her husband, Herman C. Dekker, preceded her in death on September 11, 1991. The scholarship is provided to assist associate degree students seeking a major in the Fine Arts.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
