/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 516 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of the friends and colleagues of Harriett M. Reid, who established the Harriett M. Reid Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Harriett Reid had a long career at Muskegon Public Schools as a counselor, gym instructor, and coach. Following her retirement, Harriett's friends and colleagues at Muskegon Public Schools established, in her honor, a fund they were confident would be properly managed by the Community Foundation. Harriett's wish is that the scholarship be used to benefit students who reflect the great ethnic and cultural diversity of Muskegon Public Schools. This Scholarship thus heightens Harriett's lifelong commitment to education by granting community youth the lasting gift of education.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
769 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 516 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Gerhard \(Gary\) Olsen, who established the Gerhard O. and Doris E. Olsen Memorial Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Gerhard \(Gary\) Olsen, a prosperous businessman in the Muskegon area, wanted to thank the people who helped him succeed in life. He was given a very special gift as a child by Andrew and Clara Andersen. It was the gift of love, family, and home. When Gary lost his parents within a couple of years of each other, he was young and alone in the world. The Andersens were not people of means. Andrew was the long-term Custodian at Muskegon High School, but they would not sit by and let a child founder. They welcomed him into their home, where he grew up as a brother to their son, who was close to Gary's age. He thanks and honors the Andersens with this.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
