/P 517 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Peggy Elliott and Hugh Campbell, who established the Hugh and Peg Campbell Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County in memory of Peg Campbell. Margaretha \(Peg\) Campbell graduated from Muskegon High School, and her husband, Hugh, from Muskegon Heights High School. They went on to raise seven children here. In Peg's memory, Hugh and their daughter, Peggy, have established the Hugh and Peg Campbell Scholarship Fund. Peg was active in sports at a time when women were not encouraged to pursue them. She especially loved softball and played for several years for the Muskegon Lassies, part of the All-American Girls Professional Baseball League. Hugh and Peg have already been generous in giving back to the community, as evidenced by the Peg Campbell Soccer Field at Muskegon Catholic High School, the playground at Laketon Township, and the scholarship at GMI Kettering, where Hugh received his education before founding Campbell Grinder Company.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [16]
>>
