810 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 519 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of the friends and family of James E. Newton, who established the James E. Newton Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. James E. Newton was born in Muskegon and served as an aerospace engineer for NASA. He believed that men and women of science needed to use their skills "for the positive advancement of humankind, not the demise of mankind." At the age of 27, Jim died suddenly of a heart attack. Following his death, Jim's mother, Hester, learned about the Scholarship Program at the Community Foundation and thought it was a fitting way to create a scholarship in Jim's honor. James Newton valued intelligence and learning, and, accordingly, all gifts given in his memory have contributed to the James E. Newton Scholarship. Hester Newton desires that these scholarships inspire young people to stay in school and help them recognize, as her son Jim did, that the lasting gift of knowledge is one to be treasured.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
