/P 519 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of James Mullally, who established the James Mullally Scholarship of the Muskegon County Community Foundation. James Mullally and his family, long-time residents of Muskegon, have established a tradition of giving in the Laketon Township area. The Mullally family gift to that community, Mullally Field, still offers recreational enjoyment to residents and visitors. James Mullally maintained his family's tradition of giving by naming the Community Foundation in his will. With his gift, the James Mullally Scholarship was established to support Reeths-Puffer graduates residing in Laketon Township. To the credit of James Mullally and his family, the youth of the community they loved will continue to benefit from the lasting gift of education.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
