/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of the family of James P. Jackson, who established the James P. Jackson Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. This Fund was established by Steve Jackson and his sister, Sue Jackson, with proceeds from their mother's trust. It is named in honor of a beloved husband and father. James earned a degree from the University of Detroit and has worked in the accounting field throughout his career. Scholarships will be awarded to graduating seniors of Muskegon County High Schools pursuing an Accounting degree. This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of the family of James P. Jackson, who established the James P. Jackson Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. This Fund was established by Steve Jackson and his sister, Sue Jackson, with proceeds from their mother's trust. It is named in honor of a beloved husband and father. James earned a degree from the University of Detroit and has worked in the accounting field throughout his career. Scholarships will be awarded to graduating seniors of Muskegon County High Schools pursuing an Accounting degree.)
