/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Clarke Manning, who established the Jean and Clarke Manning Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County in honor of his wife, Jean. Jean Manning's life's passion was music, especially string music, and her beloved violin. Jean played with orchestras, often as concertmaster, in Jackson, Saginaw, Grand Rapids, and, for thirty-eight years, the West Shore Symphony. Her greatest love was sharing music with children, which she did for many years in the public schools and as a private teacher. Established by her husband, Clarke, this scholarship fund will ensure that Jean's love for music continues long into the future.)
