837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 520 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Dr. Helen Barnard and J. Fred Boyd, who established the J. Fred and Helen Barnard Boyd Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Dr. Helen Barnard Boyd was one of the first women to attend the University of Michigan Medical School and was also Muskegon's first female doctor. J. Fred Boyd was a prominent Muskegon businessman. They shared a commitment to youth and education, and often took troubled young people into their home to give them a second chance in life. In the 1960s, these two Muskegon patrons established a private foundation, which they incorporated with the Community Foundation for Muskegon County in the early 1970's. Since its creation and because of its tremendous impact, hundreds of Muskegon students have received awards that have helped them with their education. Dr. Helen Barnard and J. Fred Boyd lived long and fruitful lives. Through this, they have left a permanent legacy for Muskegon-area youth.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
