/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Joyce Singerling, who established the Judith G. Singerling and John J. Singerling, Sr. Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Judith Singerling loved education. She was salutatorian of the first graduating class at Reeths-Puffer High School and received her undergraduate degree from Eastern Michigan University and her Master's of Education from the University of Michigan. After she retired from the Lansing school system in 1999, she became an active community volunteer and remained an avid U of M fan. Her civic involvement was inherited from her father, John, who served on the Reeths-Puffer School Board for 18 years, volunteered with the Muskegon Township Fire Dept., and was active in many other community organizations. This fund will support Reeths-Puffer graduates pursuing their higher education dreams.)
