/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Lila E. and Norma J. DeYoung, who established the Keith R. DeYoung Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Lila and Norma DeYoung established this fund to honor the memory of their only brother, Keith DeYoung, who died on February 2, 1998, their father's birthday, and was a champion of quality education for children in the Muskegon area. Life-long Muskegon residents who still live in the family home in which they were raised, Lila and Norma worked side by side at Sealed Power for 43 years each, one handling the hourly payroll and the other, the salaried payroll. They are active members of St. Paul's Episcopal Church and the Angell Neighborhood Association and volunteers for many other organizations. Loyal in everything they do, caring, gentle, and unassuming, we welcome Norma and Lila DeYoung to the foundation family.)
