/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Wyart and Annie Green, who established the Mother Davis, Wyart, and Annie Satcher Green Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. WMUS radio personality Mattie Wesley Davis, known as "Mother Davis," so inspired North Muskegon residents Wyart and Annie Green that they established a college scholarship in her name to benefit underprivileged students. Wyart Green first heard the kind voice of Mother Davis while visiting Muskegon in the 1960s. The "Heavenly Echoes" radio gospel personality had such an impact on Green and his wife, Annie, that they wanted to honor the woman known for her motto: "Get up, get dressed, and make your way to the house of the Lord.")
