/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Reverend Keith Pohl, who established the Muskegon Heights High School Alumni Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Rev. Keith Pohl, who graduated from Muskegon Heights High School in 1952 and valued his education there, desired to give back to the students of the school to which he was indebted. Though he has been gone from the community for many years, he had a passion for and felt indebted to the Heights and the U of M, from which he graduated. Being a Methodist minister and having attended Temple United Methodist Church years ago, he approached the church to establish a scholarship fund. Temple United Methodist Church, recognizing that the Community Foundation could administer this program more effectively, established this fund to provide scholarships for Heights graduates and residents to attend the University of Michigan.)
