/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Norine M. Clark, who established the Norine Clark Family Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Norine spent over 30 years teaching in Ravenna elementary schools, leaving lasting impressions on her students. She loved reading, taught music on piano and organ, and was involved in her church. Their family owned a blueberry farm, and her husband, Wayne, served as a township supervisor and a member of the Blueberry Association board. The scholarship supports graduating seniors from Ravenna High School pursuing degrees in agriculture or teaching, carrying on the Clark family legacy.)
