/P 532 0 R
/E (This scholarship was established by Maureen Campbell through the Community Foundation for Muskegon County in memory of her husband, Norman J. Campbell. A graduate of Muskegon Heights High School and the University of Michigan, Norman was a mechanical engineer who worked on the SR-71 Blackbird at Lockheed before continuing his career with General Electric. He later returned to Muskegon to help lead the family business, Campbell Grinder Company, serving as president until his retirement in 2001. Known for treating employees like family, Norman valued hard work, humility, and time with loved ones. This scholarship supports students attending the University of Michigan, with preference given to engineering majors and secondary consideration to nursing students.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [8]
