/P 532 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Bertha DeVette, who established the Paul DeVette Education Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Paul DeVette was a respected educator in the Muskegon Public Schools for 32 years, serving as Principal at Nelson School and as a teacher at Steele Junior High School before his retirement in 1962. His wife, Bertha, established the Paul DeVette Education to honor his memory. Paul DeVette's many friends, fellow educators, and former students also contributed to this scholarship in his memory. The award provides scholarships to graduating Muskegon High School seniors who plan to pursue a career in teaching and who hope to uphold the exemplary standard set by Paul DeVette's commitment to teaching.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [16]
