/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 533 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Barbara Kutches, who established the Peter J. and Barbara J. Kutches Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Pete and Barbara Kutches are well-known figures in the Muskegon area, even though they both grew up in Escanaba. Pete was a coach in the area stretching over 4 decades at Muskegon High School, Muskegon Catholic Central, and finally Reeths-Puffer before retiring in the late 1990s. He was best known as a football coach, winning state championships as a head coach at MCC and R-P, the only coach in the state of Michigan to do so. Barbara worked as a nurse at Mercy Hospital for several years, serving as the director of nursing. They shared 62 years of marriage, 5 children, 15 grandchildren, and soon-to-be 15 great-grandchildren. Pete was the 10th of 13 kids in his family, and the only one to go on to earn a college degree, thanks to a scholarship he was awarded. Because of this, Pete and Barbara both felt strongly that they wanted to provide that opportunity to area youth, specifically in the areas in which they felt rewarded in their careers - education, and nursing.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
