1082 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 534 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Barbara Arter, who established the Richard and Barbara Arter Fine Arts Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County in memory of Dick Arter. This fund was established following Dick Arter's unexpected death while wintering in Arizona. He was Vice President of Howmet Corporation until his retirement. He was an active member of Community United Methodist Church and a past President of the Reeths-Puffer Board of Education and United Way. Before Barbara's retirement, she taught sixth grade at Orchard View School and is now an active community volunteer, particularly faithful to McMillan School's "Adopt-A-Reader" program. Because they have long been loyal supporters of the Reeths-Puffer Schools, Mrs. Arter established this fund to assist Reeths-Puffer students in their study of fine arts at a college or summer camp.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [10]
>>
