/P 535 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Augusta A. Moran, who established the Robert F. and Augusta A. Moran, RN Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Robert and Augusta Moran were ordinary people who lived ordinary lives. Bob Moran retired as a yard master for the C & O Railroad after 40 years of service, and Gussie Moran was a homemaker who also worked as a clerk at Parson's Clothing in Muskegon Heights. Together, they enjoyed small-game hunting, sport fishing, and all that the outdoors had to offer. In fact, Robert Moran spent a great deal of time showing young people how to enjoy these activities safely and responsibly. They believed deserving people who are given a break can succeed. This scholarship, established with a bequest following Mrs. Moran's death, will assist those who "may be in the middle of the class but have the desire, determination, and the aptitude to be a nurse.")
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [10]
>>
