1152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (This scholarship has been made possible by the generosity of Barbara Reese, who established the Tom Reese and Richard T. and Mary Reese Scholarship of the Community Foundation for Muskegon County. Mary Kiser Reese grew up in Ashland, Kentucky, 4th of 10 children. When she was 14, both of her parents died, making it necessary for her to quit school and get a job to contribute to the family income and, along with her older siblings, raise the younger children. After all of them were grown, Mary moved to Niagara Falls, N.Y., to live with an older sister and found employment in a department store where she met her husband, Richard Reese. They were married before he went into the Army, and he served his country during WWII in the 3rd Armored Tank Brigade. After the war, he was employed with Hooker Chemical, and Tom was born in 1947. In 1954, they were transferred to Montague with other employees when Hooker built the plant here on Whitbeck Road. They bought a house on White Lake, where Tom grew up, and his parents spent the rest of their lives. They saved money for their son Tom to go to college. Tom graduated from Montague High School and went on to Michigan Tech, where he earned his engineering degree. He then worked at Howmet until his retirement in 2009.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [10]
>>
